wepoll 1.5.8 (2020-06-29), vendored for the VM's poller on Windows
=================================================================

Source: https://github.com/piscisaureus/wepoll, tag v1.5.8, commit
0598a791bf9c, from the dist files at that tag.

Copied unmodified:

  LICENSE
  wepoll.c, wepoll.h

wepoll gives Windows an epoll interface over the AFD driver's socket polling,
level-triggered or one-shot. The VM's poller (src/proc/poll.c) watches each
socket one-shot and arms it again whenever a reader or writer finds it not
ready, which is the edge-triggered behaviour the other systems' pollers have.

The build (vm/Makefile) compiles it on Windows only, as upstream intends,
without this project's warning flags, into the VM's archive.
